# Coding standards

- `ruff check rodeo tests` — zero warnings
- Public functions: typed params and return types
- No dead code, commented-out blocks, or TODO in committed code
- Polling: `self._sleep()` — never `time.sleep()`
- Helm: always `helm upgrade --install` — never `helm install`
- kubectl JSON: heredoc (SSH) or `input=` (subprocess) — never `echo | kubectl`
- Instruqt + hosts with AAAA: `curl -4` in shell tasks — do not use `get_url` for those URLs
- Secrets in plans: keep `??key` — never rewrite to `??env:` (CI-only form)

## CI / local gate

```bash
ruff check rodeo tests
pytest tests/ -v
```

Never push with failing tests or ruff warnings.
